{
  "name": "embershot",
  "description": "embershot is an experimental Rust-based runtime implementing a pure, lazy combinator calculus via an eval/apply transition system inspired by the Spineless Tagless G-machine. Developed for the ICFP Programming Contest 2020, it features a custom, non-moving concurrent garbage collector named 'incinerator' based on the Ueno-Ohori algorithm. The system prioritizes graph reduction and thunk management over high-level language features, providing a low-level substrate for functional program execution.",
